<title>USA: Paul Revere Corp Q3 shr loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Paul Revere Corp Q3 shr loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>WORCESTER, Mass. 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr	loss	    $4.98   profit	 $0.48</p>
<p> Net	loss	  224,200   profit	21,800</p>
<p> Revs			   n/a			n/a</p>
<p> Avg shrs		     n/a			n/a</p>
<p>	  Nine months</p>
<p> Shr	loss	    $4.04   profit	 $1.43</p>
<p> Net	loss	  181,700   profit	64,500</p>
<p> Revs			   n/a			n/a</p>
<p> Avg shrs		     n/a			n/a</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES: The company said the quarter loss is due to a $244.3 million after-tax reserve strengthening ($5.43 per common share) in the individual disability insurance segment.</p>
<p>Results also include after-tax net realized investment gains of $6.2 million ($0.14 per common share) in the 1996 third quarter and $4.6 million ($0.10 per common share) in the 1995 third quarter.</p>
